Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 14:50:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03479/11362] [outer-loop] #2 result: energy-as-fitness QD
 nulls on hard tail -> crossover starved of shared states

Ran experiment_2_energy_as_fitness_qd on the hard tail. On wa30/sb26 (BFS FAILS,
genuinely hard) QD ALSO fails; su15 is BFS-solvable. QD-generates-where-BFS-fails=0/3.
Both #1 (perception-gated heuristic) and #2 (energy-as-fitness QD) first-drafts null on
the hard games.

DIAGNOSIS: the non-AR crossover-at-shared-visited-state operator almost never fires --
random seed trajectories on large state spaces diverge immediately and rarely share a
visited state, so QD degrades to mutation-only random search and fails like BFS. FIX:
Go-Explore return-then-explore seeding (deliberately revisit archived states) to create
the shared-state structure crossover needs. Next: instrument crossover fire-rate +
swap random seeding for Go-Explore seeding.

verdict: complete: energy_as_fitness_qd_no_winner_honest_null_gap_sharpened

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
